      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was going to suggest that there\u0027s a better name for this, based on the actual encoding type in the spec. That led me to re-discover a rabbit hole of Lab stuff, so I\u0027m not sure the math here is technically correct.\n\nFixed point Lab values use a different range, depending on which TAG they\u0027re in. Relevant paragraph from `10.10 lut16Type`:\n\n    For colour values that are in the PCSLAB colour space on the PCS side of\n    the tag, this tag uses the legacy 16-bit PCSLAB encoding defined in Tables\n    42 and 43, not the 16-bit PCSLAB encoding defined in 6.3.4.2. This encoding\n    is retained for backwards compatibility with profile version 2. The PCSLAB\n    L* values have a different encoding than the PCSLAB a* and PCSLAB b* values.\n    \nAh, wait - are we only using this to build PCSLAB values in an mAB or mBA tag? I\u0027m getting myself confused - the legacy encoding may only be for one-dimensional LUTs?",
